===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[instance]] of [[#Verb|overrun]]ning.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013 June 18|author=w:Simon Romero|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/19/world/americas/brazilian-leaders-brace-for-more-protests.html|title=Protests Widen as Brazilians Chide Leaders|journal=New York Times|text=Some of the stadiums being built for the World Cup soccer tournament, scheduled for next year, have also been criticized for delays and cost '''overruns''', and have become subjects of derision as protesters question whether they will become white elephants.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=December 13 2021|author=Molly Ball; Jeffrey Kluger; Alejandro de la Garza|title=Elon Musk: Person of the Year 2021|journal=Time Magazine|url=https://time.com/person-of-the-year-2021-elon-musk/|text=Tesla’s first decade was plagued by unmet deadlines, technical snafus and cost '''overruns'''.}}
# The amount by which something [[#Verb|overrun]]s.
#: {{ux|en|At least this year's '''overrun''' isn't as unmanageable as last year!}}
# {{lb|en|aviation}} An area of [[terrain]] beyond the end of a [[runway]] that is kept [[flat]] and [[unobstructed]] to allow an [[aircraft]] that runs off the end of the runway to [[stop]] safely.
#: {{ux|en|The runway has 7,000 feet of paved surface, plus a 2,000-foot grass '''overrun'''.}}
# {{lb|en|food}} [[air|Air]] that is [[whip]]ped into a [[frozen]] [[dessert]] to make it easier to serve and eat.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Wayne Gisslen|title=Professional Baking|page=497|text=If ice cream has too much '''overrun''', it will be airy and foamy and will lack flavor.}}

